From: Egor Ignatov <egori@altlinux.org>
Date: Thu, 23 Jan 2025 20:44:13 +0300
Subject: fs/xfs: Handle root inode read failure in grub_xfs_mount
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Signed-off-by: Egor Ignatov <egori@altlinux.org>
FG: Cherry-picked from
https://lore.kernel.org/grub-devel/20250123174415.1251915-1-egori@altlinux.org/
with feedback folded in
Signed-off-by: Fabian Grünbichler <f.gruenbichler@proxmox.com>
---
 grub-core/fs/xfs.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/grub-core/fs/xfs.c b/grub-core/fs/xfs.c
index 4034062..08bc66a 100644
--- a/grub-core/fs/xfs.c
+++ b/grub-core/fs/xfs.c
@@ -1052,6 +1052,8 @@ grub_xfs_mount (grub_disk_t disk)
 	       grub_cpu_to_be64(data->sblock.rootino));
 
   grub_xfs_read_inode (data, data->diropen.ino, &data->diropen.inode);
+  if (grub_errno != GRUB_ERR_NONE)
+    goto fail;
 
   return data;
  fail:
